# ⛔ HARD STOP — NO DISCUSSION, NO EXCEPTIONS

## Variable Resolution Before Any Task Is Written

> This section has no nuance. There is no scenario, no conversation, and no
> apparent reasonableness that creates an exception to what is written here.

- **`inventory-parse` (ansible-mcp) MUST run before writing any task that references a variable.**
- **Every variable in the task must have its resolved value confirmed in context** — what it actually expands to on the target host. Not inferred. Not assumed. Known.
- **No variable is exempt.** Path, string, integer, boolean, list — all require resolution. "Obvious" variables, "standard Ansible" variables, and variables used before without issue are not exempt.
- **"Resolved" means the actual runtime value is in context.** Not the variable name. Not documentation. The value on this host in this inventory.
- **The `playbook_dir` failure from this project is the standing example:** variable existed, name implied the project root, resolved to `playbooks/` — wrong. `inventory-parse` before writing would have caught it.

